---
source: crates/dreamd-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "subcommand_help(\"setup\")"
---
Front door: scaffold .agent/ (via init) and print the harness wiring next steps

Usage: setup [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -y, --yes
          Accept defaults without prompting. `setup` never prompts today, so this is accepted and ignored; the interactive wizard ships in a follow-up

      --harness <HARNESS>
          Harness(es) to wire up: `claude` writes .mcp.json, `cursor` writes .cursor/mcp.json, `both` writes both, `none` writes neither
          
          [default: both]
          [possible values: claude, cursor, both, none]

      --no-write-mcp
          Do not write any harness MCP config

      --force
          Replace an existing `mcpServers.dreamd` entry that does not run `npx -y dreamd-mcp`. Other MCP servers are preserved. Does not override a config file that is not valid JSON

      --start-watch
          Start the shared daemon after scaffolding. Parsed now; `setup` still only prints the `dreamd watch` command

      --no-start-watch
          Only print the `dreamd watch` command instead of starting it (default)

      --dry-run
          Print the planned actions without writing anything

  -h, --help
          Print help
